"""Recurring source-perturbation investigation guidance, not its scoring sheet."""

PERTURBATION_TASK = """Investigate what changing the supplied molecule establishes about its contribution to an observed outcome. Discover relevant intervention experiments through the available literature, sequence identity lookup and NCBI Entrez study searches, including GEO and SRA. Establish the relationship between the supplied sequence and each actual experimental subject, including strain, construct and changed region. Decide whether the published measurements resolve the comparison or whether analyzing deposited data would address a specific missing comparison or uncertainty. Select available acquisition and analysis operations for that scientific purpose and request further work when it would improve the assessment.

Establish the actual recipient background, donor molecule or construct, changed copy, coexisting same-protein copies and distinct required partners, reference and intervention arms, intended change, conditions and controls. A reference construct called WT is not automatically a native wild-type organism. Reconstitution in a component-free recipient, replacement by a variant, a protein-domain truncation and native gene deletion followed by restoration are different experiments. When descriptions differ, first identify which experiment and arm each describes. Distinguish an unverified correspondence from incompatible claims about the same tested subject; descriptions of separate strains do not themselves establish a conflict.

Describe introduced genetic material as an experimental change to the tested construct. A transposon insertion does not establish that the native gene is itself a mobile element. Retain control and design facts in anchored observations and condition/context references attached to the contribution assessment; each source_claim predicate and value must describe its named subject.

A source_subjects entry names a source entity without attaching sequence bytes. source.sequence.scan compares source text with the supplied sequence but does not create a sequence reference. Observations with operand_intervals require subjects whose sequence bytes are available; public.ncbi.sequence can acquire such a reference for a selected accession and version. Inspect the returned sequence_ref before using it as that operand. An extracted observation still needs its exact source anchor. An exact database-sequence match establishes correspondence to that reference; the experiment's actual strain and construct require their own evidence.

Under the received-scientific-finding progress binding, retain newly established or corrected experimental information through the ordinary reasoning action: a source-bound observation and an assessment with investigation_finding. Describe the result for the actual tested molecule and conditions, then qualify what it establishes about the supplied hypothesis. Anchor the observation in the original experiment or acquired analysis result and use the numerical sheets as supporting calculations. Useful findings include negative results and demonstrated limits on interpretation even when the final evidence ratio is unavailable. Apply the existing finding equivalence and replacement fields across repeated paper/dataset representations and corrections. When rereading only changes your interpretation of an existing source claim, identify the earlier finding with same_source_claim_as_ref and use replaces_refs when correcting it. A narrower quotation or different wording does not establish another experiment or measurement. When commissioning a child to investigate such findings, request changed_assessment_refs alongside the required numerical fields so its parent receives those reasoning records.

Link acquired GEO/SRA files to their source study, sample, experimental arm, biological replicate, preparation, time and measured endpoint. Retain reference genome and annotation versions, mapping and preprocessing choices, quality measurements, normalization, comparison direction and shared controls. Select TnSeq reference, protocol, recipe and contrasts from the documented design and the service's currently available options. Existing execution episodes submit, monitor and acquire results; the dedicated TnSeq result adapter exposes retained TRANSIT tables. Use the RNASeq route for expression measured after a defined intervention, preserving which molecule was changed and which transcripts responded. A downstream response can establish a conditional contribution while leaving the mechanism unresolved. Check actual service availability; a packaged application definition alone does not prove execution is currently possible.

When AppService is configured, the main literature investigation can commission the existing launch and results roles. Use literature.intervention_analysis.contract when available to construct the native adapter and requested_schema from your explicit document and field selections. Put those returned values into the existing results selector; its requirement IDs must match the selected document bindings. Request bvbrc_application_outcomes in the results child's typed report. Keep the submitted sample/condition map, reference, recipe and contrast with the acquired task results. Request native records with their measurements and source_location members through bvbrc_application_outcomes. The received_intervention_analysis_rows context contains the actual admitted fields. Select those operands with application_analysis using the received publication sheet_ref, field identifier, representation, row_ordinal, exact feature_id and metric. A directly acquired deposited table instead uses native_analysis with its source_ref. For both routes, provide source-backed experimental_design and sample_bindings, including the exact sample-to-file correspondence and biological versus technical units. These selectors read retained values; prediction operands still require independent source support.

Retain screen effects, insertion means, log fold changes, p/q values and uncertainty on their native scales. A p/q value is neither estimate variance nor a function probability. A signed or logarithmic effect cannot populate the restoration calculator's nonnegative endpoint means. Preserve restoration components as separate diagnostics.

For the final evidence ratio, first state the two competing claims about this molecule's contribution. The effect operand is what the experiment actually measured. The assertion_prediction and alternative_prediction operands are what each claim predicts the experiment would measure, expressed for that same endpoint, contrast, scale, unit and conditions. Identify where each expected value comes from and which calculation choices it depends on. The prediction_model field selects how measurement uncertainty enters the comparison: a normal or Student-t distribution with the declared variance interpretation. It does not generate either expected value or select a biological model. The prediction and the observation may appear in the same paper: establish whether the prediction was calculated without using the outcome now being assessed to tune it. Copying that outcome into a prediction would manufacture agreement. A comparison of models of whole-cell behavior supports a claim about this molecule only when the intervention and controls establish that attribution. Use the existing evidence-ratio calculation when these expected values, the variance of the measured estimate and the selected measurement model are supported. Missing predictions, variance, model support or subject correspondence leave the corresponding score unresolved; retain the measured effect and the experimental conclusion with their limitations.

Use the reusable intervention_response assessment type for deletion, inhibition, replacement, reconstitution and restoration experiments. Their design determines which numerical comparisons are meaningful; a new molecule, paper or source format does not need a new scoring template. When recording an experiment assessment, supply experiment_assessment with the received source-backed assay reference, stable assessment_key, scientific question, conclusion and limitations. Keep that experiment_ref across representations and corrections. A correction names the latest revises_sheet_ref and explains its revision_reason. Historical inputs and conclusions remain in their saved sheets. Several questions may concern one experiment; they do not create independent experiments. Unknown experiment identity remains unresolved in the raw measurement sheet until source evidence establishes it.

To find a previous assessment, use its sheet_ref from received cells or inspect Source records whose provider is literature.a106.intervention_grading. state.query with kind=source reads source metadata; its references filter follows metadata links such as parent_source_refs and does not search the worksheet bytes for experiment_ref. Read the selected sheet with source.read, or locate the literal experiment_assessment with source.locate and read that part of the sheet. Check its experiment_ref, assessment_key and revision chain before updating the assessment. A source-metadata query with no matches does not establish that no assessment exists.

Assessments with different assessment_key values can concern the same experiment without revising each other. Follow the explicit revises_sheet_ref chain to establish which assessment is superseded; creation order alone does not establish a revision. When changing a final worksheet's selection between different assessment questions, explain that choice and its relevance to the final question. Describe the actual change in revision_reason without calling a separately keyed assessment superseded. Select the original experiment only once.

Identify the actual measured endpoint, eligibility denominator, normalization, time origin and sampling time, calibration, detection limits and uncertainty. Compare arms only within supported endpoint and condition scopes. A visible PCR product does not supply calibrated events per cell, and nondetection is not zero. Similar bands or a nonsignificant difference do not establish numerical equivalence. A signature-residue substitution is not a measured catalytic-null state. Keep measured protein signal, molecular amount and relevant activity separate. Look for reported expression and abundance controls before calling them absent. Retain what they measured and which conditions and sampling times they cover, including useful controls whose applicability to another endpoint remains uncertain.

Find source-supported numerical reference, perturbed and restored outcomes when they exist. Do not invent a restoration arm or borrow another endpoint to complete a triple. Nominate a measured nuisance amount comparison outside the intended change separately from actual endpoint-scale bounds on alternative explanations for perturbation and restoration. Intended depletion is not a second nuisance penalty; matching conditions do not prove effect isolation. Preserve shared controls, lysates, calibration and physical measurement identities without assuming independence. Complementary assembly or binding experiments address named limitations and are not automatically independent phenotype replications.

For every measured arm, retain the reported statistic, the scale on which it was summarized, its spread type and scale, the repetition count and what was repeated. A logarithmic display does not establish that the mean or SD was calculated on a logarithmic scale. Keep SD, SEM, confidence intervals, detection limits and untyped plus-minus values distinct. Group technical readings within their actual biological or preparation unit; descriptive means and variability can be useful even when sampling independence is unknown. A standard error calculated from SD needs a supported independent-unit basis. Reported SEM retains its source interpretation. Preserve pairing, shared controls and covariance between mean estimates; unknown covariance is not zero. Pixel-reading constraints remain separate from sampling uncertainty. Do not discard a useful displayed estimate merely because some statistical metadata is unresolved.

To locate methods or tables in a PDF, use source.pdf.info to read its physical page count. source.pdf.text accepts page as the first page and optional last_page as the inclusive end, so you can extract a relevant range or the whole document and search the retained text with source.locate. The text retains page breaks; its byte offsets belong to that derivative, not the PDF. Use physical PDF page numbers when requesting an original page view, rather than assuming printed page labels match them.

When extracted table text leaves a row, column, strain or unit label uncertain, use the available original-page or image viewers to inspect the layout. Check the headings and caption before assigning a value to an experimental arm, and retain the page/image source used to resolve that assignment. Text extraction alone does not establish whether a discrepancy is in the publication or was introduced during extraction. If the original view is unavailable or still ambiguous, retain the unresolved assignment with the otherwise usable measurements.

For reported arm summaries in source text or a table, literature.perturbation.populate accepts source_measurements with data_source_ref=null. Select exact number spans and the printed endpoint-unit header, retaining each arm's summary, spread, repetition count, unit of replication and the passages explaining those meanings. Supply null for absent arms. The optional covariances list retains reported covariance between mean estimates with its exact number and squared endpoint unit, or a selected uncorrelated relationship with the passage and interpretation basis that justify it. Replication within each arm does not establish independence between arms. Missing pairs remain unknown. The reader obtains every number from the selected source and uses the existing summary calculations. Existing retained measurement files still use data_source_ref. Neither route creates prediction numbers.

For an existing literature.perturbation.populate sheet, request literature_perturbation_operand_cells through requested_perturbation_operand_components. These are the original saved measurements with their identities and uncertainty meanings. Use reference_endpoint, perturbed_endpoint or restored_endpoint as native_endpoint; use perturbation_difference (W-K) or restoration_difference (R-K) as endpoint_difference. Match W_mean_variance, K_mean_variance or R_mean_variance to its endpoint, or perturbation_mean_variance/restoration_mean_variance to its contrast in the same sheet. The original point and summary return formats remain distinct; receiving one does not provide unrequested operands from another. Restoration indices and covariance bounds do not supply an effect variance. Preserve unknown uncertainty and the distinction between technical and biological units.

For a printed table number with a separate unit header, literature.intervention_grading.populate accepts source_table_number. Select the number, row_label, column_labels and unit from the retained HTML/JATS table. Include both a grouped quantity header and its model subheader when those together identify the column. The reader checks their positions and retains the original number identity. Use this to read published model predictions without treating them as observed experimental arms. Reading a number does not establish whether the prediction was fitted to this observation, whether its baseline and conditions apply, or whether the comparison isolates this molecule's contribution. Keep those questions explicit in the experimental assessment. The source_number shortcut continues to require a unit directly beside the number.

For published specific-activity measurements with a shared table-header unit, use the existing literature.measurement_comparison.populate reader. Its received literature_measurement_comparison_cells can supply native_left/native_right or converted_left/converted_right as native_endpoint, protocol_difference as endpoint_difference, and protocol_ratio as endpoint_ratio. A difference_variance is uncertainty for protocol_difference from that same sheet; it requires supported joint estimator covariance. The reader does not infer covariance from SD and a repetition count. Standardized discrepancies, common-mean combinations and sensitivity scenarios are not intervention effects. The A106 design, attribution, subject correspondence and independent-prediction criteria still apply to these measurements.

Interpret the source design and nominate supported operands; deterministic readers and calculators perform arithmetic. In interpretations.support_refs and prediction_model.support_refs, cite received reference records with exact source anchors, such as experiment_ref or separately anchored control/method references. A document's source_ref alone does not supply an anchored interpretation witness. Unknown criteria can retain an empty support list. Preserve usable native data and explicit scientific unknowns when a source cannot populate a numerical component. The source restoration index is a proposed conditional combination, not a probability, target correspondence, annotation credit or investigation-progress reward. Do not convert paper labels, repetition counts or descriptive selected-event fractions into an overall reliability grade. Return only the parent's requested typed components and necessary experimental qualifications."""

A106_PARENT_TASK = """For A106 intervention evidence, determine what changing the supplied molecule establishes about its contribution to an observed outcome. Commission literature investigations with the supplied sequence or other material, the biological question and the information needed for your next decision. Each child discovers relevant studies, establishes correspondence to the actual strain and construct, reads the experimental design and chooses its own acquisition and analysis operations. Your own operation catalog defines the work available at this parent level.

The A106 path is source or analysis measurements → intervention_response assessment → literature.a106.finalize → requested literature_a106_subscore_cells. Request the applicable literature_intervention_grading_cells when their operands and design are needed to interpret the final result. Finalization uses the existing signed log evidence ratio with explicit competing predictions and uncertainty. One experiment contributes once; summing several experiments requires supported conditional independence. Preserve unavailable values, opposing results, measured effects and unresolved assumptions. A restoration index remains a separate diagnostic.

When a child investigates new or corrected scientific findings, request changed_assessment_refs alongside the needed numerical fields. These return its ordinary reasoning assessments with investigation_finding, including qualified or negative findings. Numerical worksheet rows alone do not return those scientific assessments. Interpret the received findings for the supplied hypothesis, preserving their source subjects, conditions, equivalence and correction history. A new sheet or an opinion-only revision does not create scientific progress.

The child decides whether published results suffice or analysis of deposited data would resolve a specific uncertainty. Available literature, sequence identity and study searches provide discovery leads; GEO/SRA acquisition and configured TnSeq/RNASeq execution support dataset work. Preserve sample and file correspondence, reference versions, contrasts, replication, uncertainty and controls. Use the actual configured capabilities and service availability when commissioning that work.

Keep the experiment identity across its paper, dataset, analysis and assessment revisions. Have follow-up work use the received current assessment and retain the exact subject, assertion, alternative and biological scope when revising a final result. A new biological question has its own scope. Integrate the actual admitted return, including its limitations, before selecting further work. The configured continuation controller remains responsible for continuation."""

__all__ = ['PERTURBATION_TASK', 'A106_PARENT_TASK']
